[96.3451, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\n  ◇ careful auto · mentions production and a deploy\r\n"]
[132.7025, "o", "◆ explored · read __init__.py, cart.py, catalog.py +1 · listed shop\r\n\r\n"]
[132.9208, "o", "Three concrete production deployment risks in the shop code:\r\n\r\n"]
[135.7237, "o", "1. **Floating-point money calculations** – Both `tax.py` (`round(cents * (1 + RATE))`) and `discounts.py` (`int(total * (1 - RATES[code]))`) use floating-point arithmetic for monetary values. Although the catalog avoids floats, tax and discount calculations reintroduce them, risking rounding errors that could cause off-by-one cent discrepancies in totals.\r\n\r\n"]
[136.6468, "o", "2. **Unvalidated quantity input** – `Cart.add()` accepts any integer `qty` (including negative or zero) without validation. Adding a negative quantity could reduce line items below zero or create negative subtotals, leading to nonsensical discount/tax results and potential inventory/accounting errors.\r\n\r\n"]
[138.1283, "o", "3. **Hardcoded, immutable catalog** – Product prices are stored in a hardcoded dictionary (`catalog.py.PRICES`). Updating prices requires code changes and redeployment, making the system inflexible for real-world scenarios where prices change frequently (e.g., sales, cost updates). This also prevents dynamic pricing or per‑customer pricing without modifying the source.\r\n"]
[138.1296, "o", "\r\n✓ 4 reads · 1 lookup · 42s · ↑33.3k ↓1.9k · ctx 4%\r\n\r\n"]
[138.1446, "o", "\u001b[?2004h\r\u001b[K› \r\u001b[2C"]
[142.8500, "o", "\r\u001b[K› \r\u001b[2C"]
